<header><p class="enc-kicker">Work / monument · text</p><h1 class="enc-title">Gelnhausen Charter</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1180</span> · <a href="/centuries/12th-century">12th century</a> · Also known as Gelnhausen Diploma</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Gelnhausen Charter was issued by Emperor <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/frederick-barbarossa">Frederick Barbarossa</a> at the diet of Gelnhausen in April 1180. It divided the confiscated Duchy of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/saxony">Saxony</a> of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/henry-the-lion">Henry the Lion</a>, granting the western part as the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/duchy-of-westphalia">Duchy of Westphalia</a> to Archbishop Philip of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cologne">Cologne</a> and the rest to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bernhard-duke-of-saxony">Bernhard of Anhalt</a>. It marked the end of the old stem duchy of Saxony.</p></div>
